(Preconditions: origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha (true), destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha (true), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (true), origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha (true), destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha (true), origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha (true), destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha (true), transport_leg_available transport_leg_alpha (true).)
(Effect: transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha, transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha, transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha, not transport_leg_available transport_leg_alpha.)
(Now goal requires transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_origin_linked, transport_leg_destination_linked. Good.)
(Now we need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha (we haven't yet). Also need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (we have not used vehicle_unit_gamma yet; it's currently available? Initially vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta only; vehicle_unit_gamma not mentioned in init, so presumably available by default? Not listed. In init we have vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha, vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta. No mention of vehicle_unit_gamma availability. It might be implicitly available? Usually if not stated, it's false. But we need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma in goal. We have not yet made it available. Initially we have candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma (true). That indicates shift_candidate_alpha is linked to vehicle_unit_gamma, which likely means vehicle_unit_gamma is allocated to shift_candidate_alpha (since candidate_vehicle_linked indicates allocation). However we also have vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true. So vehicle_unit_gamma is allocated to shift_candidate_alpha, thus not available. Goal wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true, meaning after dispatch we need vehicle_unit_gamma to become available (as effect of execute_schedule_dispatch). Indeed execute_schedule_dispatch makes vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit. So we need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha to free vehicle_unit_gamma.)
(Thus we need to execute execute_schedule_dispatch after we have dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha (true), candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma (true), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (true), and not dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (true initially). Also we need to ensure dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha is true initially? Not given; we have not mentioned dispatch_slot availability. Likely it's available by default unless allocated. We have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (true) but that does not affect availability. The dispatch_slot_available predicate is separate. Initially not mentioned; assume false? However the action allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_slot_available. We haven't allocated any dispatch slot; we have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked but not dispatch_allocated? Wait we have dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true (given). That means a dispatch slot has been allocated to shift_candidate_alpha, but we don't have the explicit predicate dispatch_allocated? Actually we have dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha in init. That likely means a dispatch slot is allocated, but we don't know which slot. However we also have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (given). So the dispatch slot allocated is dispatch_slot_alpha. The predicate dispatch_allocated indicates that a slot has been allocated; the specific link is via candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. The dispatch_slot_available predicate indicates whether the slot is free. Initially we don't have dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha; likely it's false because it's allocated. However after we execute execute_schedule_dispatch, the effect includes dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot (makes it available). So we need to dispatch to make slot available (goal requires dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha). So we need to run execute_schedule_dispatch.)
